<article class="env-lemma" id="0FT3">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0FT3">Lemma <span data-tag="0FT3">24.26.2</span>.</a> Let $(\mathcal{C}, \mathcal{O})$ be a ringed site. Let $(\mathcal{A}, \text{d})$ be a sheaf of differential graded algebras on $(\mathcal{C}, \mathcal{O})$. The full subcategory $\text{Ac}$ of the homotopy category $K(\textit{Mod}(\mathcal{A}, \text{d}))$ consisting of acyclic modules is a strictly full saturated triangulated subcategory of $K(\textit{Mod}(\mathcal{A}, \text{d}))$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Of course an object $\mathcal{M}$ of $K(\textit{Mod}(\mathcal{A}, \text{d}))$ is in $\text{Ac}$ if and only if $H^ i(\mathcal{M}) = H^0(\mathcal{M}[i])$ is zero for all $i$. The lemma follows from this, Lemma <a href="/tag/0FT2" data-tag="0FT2">24.26.1</a>, and Derived Categories, Lemma <a href="/tag/05RD" data-tag="05RD">13.6.3</a>. See also Derived Categories, Definitions <a href="/tag/05RB" data-tag="05RB">13.6.1</a> and <a href="/tag/05QM" data-tag="05QM">13.3.4</a> and Lemma <a href="/tag/05QX" data-tag="05QX">13.4.16</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>